<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldWreckScatter.xml              UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  SCALD_MECHANICS_1 build pass, S6 "burning-shallows wreck salvage" — the
  scatter half. RUT_ScaldWrecks.xml declares the three salvage buildings;
  this file places them.

  ===========================================================================
  RESOLVED, NO SUBCLASS — scald_kit_spec.md §S6, decompile this pass
  ===========================================================================
  Verse/GenStep_ScatterThings.CanScatterAt (full body read, cited in the kit
  spec and SCALD_MECHANICS_1.md's own spike-pass finding 5) walks
  GenRadial.RadialCellsAround(loc, terrainValidationRadius) and checks
  terrain.HasTag(tag) against terrainValidationAllowed — stock XML fields on
  the stock class, TAG-based rather than defName-based. So no C# subclass is
  needed: the RUT_ScaldShallow tag now carried by the three shallow
  RUT_ScaldWater* terrains (RUT_ScaldWater.xml, this same pass) is
  sufficient on its own.

  Same crib shape as JawaScrapfields.xml (this same mod, V1 row 4): a plain
  GenStepDef wrapping GenStep_ScatterThings (via RM_GenStep_ScaldWreckScatter,
  this mod's subclass that adds only the S6 Mod Settings gate: off, new maps
  scatter no wrecks), order/allowInWaterBiome/
  minSpacing/countPer10kCellsRange fields copied from that shipped,
  working precedent rather than re-derived from nothing.

  ===========================================================================
  ONE GenStepDef PER SILHOUETTE — the class field is singular
  ===========================================================================
  GenStep_ScatterThings carries one <thingDef>, not a list, so three wreck
  defs need three GenStepDefs. Each is independently terrain-validated
  against the same RUT_ScaldShallow tag, so all three only ever land on the
  Scald's own shallow water — nowhere else in the mod list carries that tag.
  This is also why the registration patch (RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml)
  can safely add all three to the GLOBAL Base_Player genSteps list rather
  than needing a biome-scoped gate: the tag itself is the scope, per the
  spec's own design (§S6: "TAG-based, not defName-based").

  ===========================================================================
  TUNING — ALL THREE VALUES INVENTED, stated plainly (no source names a wreck
  count for this mechanic)
  ===========================================================================
  countPer10kCellsRange 0.4~0.6 per silhouette (three silhouettes => a
  ceiling of roughly 6-9 attempts total on a 250x250 map, using
  JawaScrapfields.xml's own documented arithmetic: RoundToInt(size*size /
  RoundToInt(10000/value)) x GetPlacementFactor). That is a CEILING on
  ATTEMPTS, not a promise of that many wrecks: terrainValidationAllowed
  rejects every candidate cell outside the Scald's shallow band, and the
  Scald's shallows are a small fraction of any given map, so the realized
  count is expected to land well under the ceiling — "a few wrecks in the
  shallows" (§8's own wording), not a field of them. Real density is owed to
  a live/quicktest pass (no bridge access this task).
  minSpacing 6 — keeps the three silhouettes of the SAME kind from stacking
  on top of each other inside one shallow pocket; well above
  GenStep_ScatterThings' engine-hardcoded cluster radius of 4
  (JawaScrapfields.xml's own header documents this constant and the failure
  mode of setting minSpacing too close to it — this value stays clear of it).
  terrainValidationRadius 2 — covers a wreck's own 2x2 footprint plus one
  ring, so a scatter roll only lands where the whole footprint (not just its
  origin cell) sits inside the shallow band.
  allowInWaterBiome true — required; the Scald IS a water body (BiomeDef
  Lake), unlike every land biome JawaScrapfields.xml's own scatter runs on.

  order 965 — after JawaScrapfields' 960 (that step is desert-only, so no
  real interaction), well after any terrain-generation genStep so the
  RUT_ScaldWater* terrain grid (and its tags) already exists on the map when
  this step's terrain validator reads it.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RUT_Jawa_ScatterScaldWreckHull</defName>
    <order>965</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.TerminalBiomes.RM_GenStep_ScaldWreckScatter">
      <thingDef>RUT_ScaldWreckHull</thingDef>
      <allowInWaterBiome>true</allowInWaterBiome>
      <minSpacing>6</minSpacing>
      <countPer10kCellsRange>0.4~0.6</countPer10kCellsRange>
      <terrainValidationRadius>2</terrainValidationRadius>
      <terrainValidationAllowed>
        <li>RUT_ScaldShallow</li>
      </terrainValidationAllowed>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RUT_Jawa_ScatterScaldWreckTank</defName>
    <order>966</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.TerminalBiomes.RM_GenStep_ScaldWreckScatter">
      <thingDef>RUT_ScaldWreckTank</thingDef>
      <allowInWaterBiome>true</allowInWaterBiome>
      <minSpacing>6</minSpacing>
      <countPer10kCellsRange>0.4~0.6</countPer10kCellsRange>
      <terrainValidationRadius>2</terrainValidationRadius>
      <terrainValidationAllowed>
        <li>RUT_ScaldShallow</li>
      </terrainValidationAllowed>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RUT_Jawa_ScatterScaldWreckFrame</defName>
    <order>967</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.TerminalBiomes.RM_GenStep_ScaldWreckScatter">
      <thingDef>RUT_ScaldWreckFrame</thingDef>
      <allowInWaterBiome>true</allowInWaterBiome>
      <minSpacing>6</minSpacing>
      <countPer10kCellsRange>0.4~0.6</countPer10kCellsRange>
      <terrainValidationRadius>2</terrainValidationRadius>
      <terrainValidationAllowed>
        <li>RUT_ScaldShallow</li>
      </terrainValidationAllowed>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
